&lt;li&gt;Works with Delivery Assurance functions to agree how the quality and progress of a given solution delivery should be tracked and acts an expert resource to support interventions on projects where solution quality or progress has become an issue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures that appropriate standards (corporate, industry, national and international) are adhered to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with clients to evolve early solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop architecture for solutions in response to procurement requests from clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Account Management and Sales functions to ensure that key sales messages for the solutions are accurately and authoritatively communicated within bids and pitches, and to develop or qualify new opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience as an ERP Solution Architect, Enterprise Architect or Solution Design Lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise with Infor LN (formerly Baan) or a comparable enterprise ERP platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing solutions across manufacturing, warehousing, supply chain, finance and operational business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of enterprise integration architecture, middleware technologies and API-led design principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integration platforms such as Infor ION or equivalent enterprise integration technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and data integration experience, including working with complex enterprise data environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of enterprise asset management, business process management and operational technology ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating ERP solutions with platforms such as Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES), Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) tools or similar enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
