&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-113912706363268805m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coreweave.com&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re proud to be a Living Wage accredited Employer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;An Enterprise Account Executive at CoreWeave is a quota carrying, enterprise software sales position responsible for meeting and exceeding goals through generating and closing new opportunities while increasing awareness of CoreWeave in the marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Role and Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new business into the UK Enterprise &amp;amp; AI Native territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement a sales strategy aligned to regional and industry needs to help drive awareness, engagement and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focused pipeline generation on defined top target accounts/sub-sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with technology ecosystem and alliance partners to accelerate new opportunity discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage opportunities through the sales cycle from initial inquiry/outbound interaction through to forecasted pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet quarterly and annual revenue objectives for territory, whilst reporting on sales, activities, progress on a regular basis through CRM and sales forecasting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for motivated, focused, and coachable sales professionals with experience across the full spectrum of the software sales cycle – prospecting, defining and articulating value proposition, pilot process management, business case development, negotiation and closing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive SaaS or infrastructure sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent track record of success in closing business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiation, analytical, financial, and organizational capabilities. Able to thrive in an evolving, entrepreneurial structure and environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at both a tactical and strategic level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must possess a can-do, self-starter mentality in a highly collaborative atmosphere&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competence leveraging value selling frameworks such as Command of the Message and forecasting methodologies such as MEDDPICC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to AI/ML leaders and builders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love to help individuals and organizations be successful utilizing new technologies, acting as a trusted advisor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about the AI industry as a whole, the use cases organisations are deploying into production, and the technical challenges and opportunities associated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an expert in end-to-end sales process management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and provides the opportunity to develop innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for take off, the growth opportunities within the organization are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ledgy, we’re on a mission to make Europe a powerhouse of entrepreneurship by building a modern, tech-driven equity management and financial reporting platform for private and public companies. In 2026, we aim to be the leading provider for European IPOs and reporting for share-based payments. We are a value-based company with a core focus on being humble, transparent, ambitious and impactful, all in order to delivery the best experience for our customers and end users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to partner with some of the world’s leading investors. New Enterprise Associates led our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2022/09/21/ledgy-a-carta-for-european-startups-to-manage-equity-and-cap-tables-raises-22m-from-nea-sequoia-and-more/&quot;&gt;$22m Series B&lt;/a&gt; round in 2022, with Philip Chopin joining Sequoia’s Luciana Lixandru on our board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were founded in Switzerland in 2017 and today we operate globally from offices in Zurich and London. We encourage diversity and are an international team coming from 26 different countries and speaking 25 different languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Mid-level Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; at Ledgy, you’ll build reliable, scalable product experiences that help companies manage their equity with confidence. You’ll work closely with experienced engineers, product managers, and designers to turn complex equity workflows into clear, automated, user-friendly software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a strong fit if you’re ready to take ownership of well-scoped projects, grow your technical judgement, and contribute across the stack while learning from senior peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: We hire remotely across the UK, Spain, Germany, Poland, and Romania. For candidates based in London, we use a hybrid model with 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teams we are hiring for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Equity&lt;/strong&gt; — Owns the foundational logic that powers Ledgy’s equity engine. Every equity-related event — such as issuing shares, creating new pools, or adjusting ownership — generates transactions. This team defines and maintains the transaction logic, data model, and core domain behaviour that ensure Ledgy’s platform remains accurate, scalable, and compliant. They also enable employees to sell their shares seamlessly once vested.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflows &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/strong&gt; — Focuses on automating complex equity workflows and integrating with third-party services, including the trading exchange. The team builds systems that help company admins efficiently onboard and offboard employees, automate equity grants and terminations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting&lt;/strong&gt; — Transforms Ledgy’s core equity data into financial, operational, and compliance reports. The team manages large, complex datasets and ensures reporting is accurate, performant, and reliable across jurisdictions and company structures. Their work powers the insights companies and auditors rely on for decision-making and transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tax&lt;/strong&gt; — Ensures taxes are correctly reflected throughout equity operations, especially moments such as exercising, selling, mobility, and other taxable events. As a future team, Tax will build end-to-end product capabilities across the stack, helping customers manage complex tax and compliance requirements accurately across jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in the role if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience working as a Software Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable building and shipping production-quality features across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy learning complex domains and turning them into simple, maintainable product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about clean, tested, readable code and thoughtful collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are curious about equity, financial workflows, and their real-world impact on companies and employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited to grow your technical judgement through code reviews, pairing, and architecture discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of your work while asking for input early when trade-offs are unclear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack*:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a modern, cohesive stack that lets us move fast while maintaining quality:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language:&lt;/strong&gt; TypeScript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; React, Tailwind CSS, tRPC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; tRPC, Node.js, MongoDB, Temporal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; GCP, Terraform Cloud, Kubernetes, Docker, GitHub Actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*We don’t expect proficiency in this specific stack&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Your Journey Could Look Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 30 days:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be paired with an onboarding buddy who will introduce you to the world of equity management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get to know your engineering team, product managers, and designers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn how your team’s domain connects to the broader Ledgy platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up your development environment and start contributing small, well-scoped changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build familiarity with our codebase, product workflows, and engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship product features and improvements with increasing independence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with teammates to break down problems, understand trade-offs, and deliver reliable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate actively in code reviews and team discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deeper understanding of how companies manage and automate equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving quality, maintainability, and user experience in your team’s domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 6–12 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own medium-sized features from implementation through release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Design to shape pragmatic, user-centric solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical discussions around data models, workflows, and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue growing toward senior-level ownership, judgement, and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting to know you (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Meet with someone from our people team to talk about your experience and to ask questions about the role
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hackerrank take-home assessment (30-45mins) - this is a test to assess core coding cability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Coding (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; An equity domain problem to solve collaboratively using your preferred language and IDE. We want to see how &lt;strong&gt;you&lt;/strong&gt; think, so this step does not allow AI. But you can freely look up syntax questions if you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Design (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A system design session focused on practical problem-solving, clear trade-offs, and how you structure technical thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Answer behavioural style questions about your experience, using the STAR method - with a PM and EM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Interview:&lt;/strong&gt; A chance to meet one of our founders and your hiring manager for a 30-minute chat about Ledgy’s mission and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer&lt;/strong&gt; 🎉&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being part of Ledgy means:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge and re-energize with flexible working hours, 25 days of vacation, and up to 40 days of remote work from outside your home country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make space for your own professional development, with a generous yearly learning &amp;amp; development budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will receive a competitive salary + benefits + equity. All salaries are aligned with competitively benchmarked ranges based on work location and levelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For candidates based in London or Zurich we use a hybrid work model of 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ledgy, we’re on a mission to make Europe a powerhouse of entrepreneurship by building a modern, tech-driven equity management and financial reporting platform for private and public companies. In 2026, we aim to be the leading provider for European IPOs and reporting for share-based payments. We are a value-based company with a core focus on being humble, transparent, ambitious and impactful, all in order to delivery the best experience for our customers and end users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to partner with some of the world’s leading investors. New Enterprise Associates led our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2022/09/21/ledgy-a-carta-for-european-startups-to-manage-equity-and-cap-tables-raises-22m-from-nea-sequoia-and-more/&quot;&gt;$22m Series B&lt;/a&gt; round in 2022, with Philip Chopin joining Sequoia’s Luciana Lixandru on our board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were founded in Switzerland in 2017 and today we operate globally from offices in Zurich and London. We encourage diversity and are an international team coming from 26 different countries and speaking 25 different languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer on our AI Systems team, you&#39;ll build the AI foundations and product experiences of Ledgy: the Ledgy Agent, the tools and skills it runs on, our MCP server, and the platform capabilities that let other teams embed AI safely in their domains. You&#39;ll collaborate with fellow engineers, product managers, and designers in a new and fast-moving product area where correctness matters as much as speed - our customers need equity data they can trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire remotely across the UK, Spain, Germany, Poland, and Romania. For candidates based in London, we use a hybrid model with 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team you&#39;ll join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI Systems - Develops Ledgy&#39;s AI foundations and product experiences, from AI agents and AI-assisted workflows to the platform capabilities that help other teams embed AI safely in their domains. The team works in a new and evolving product area, balancing rapid iteration with reliable execution, evaluation tooling, and responsible automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help build the future of how companies manage equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy Agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system behind our in-app agent, so equity administrators can do through AI what they do manually in the app today. Ledgy Agent takes real actions and runs real analysis on live equity data, like onboarding a stakeholder end to end, and administrators depend on its accuracy and observability. You&#39;ll design the tools, skills, context, and orchestration behind it, and how it decides to handle each request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ledgy MCP.&lt;/strong&gt; Not everyone wants to open Ledgy to get things done. Our MCP server lets customers bring equity into the AI agents and tools they already use. You&#39;ll shape it alongside the in-app agent, so a capability built once works in both places, and you&#39;ll decide what we expose and how we keep it safe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measuring and improving the agent.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and build the system we use to measure the agent&#39;s quality and learn from how customers use it: evaluations, tracing, and feedback from real conversations. You decide what &quot;good&quot; means for customers, how we measure it, and how what we learn changes what we build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling.&lt;/strong&gt; The Ledgy web application, the agent, MCP, and surfaces we haven&#39;t built yet all need the same capabilities. You&#39;ll design the foundations that let us build AI features once and reuse them everywhere, and that let other teams add AI to their domains without compromising correctness. You&#39;ll also design how it runs as usage grows: the backend infrastructure, cost, and latency behind the agent and MCP, and how we keep them reliable and observable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own real parts of this and have a say in where we invest. You&#39;ll also spend time with customers to see how administrators actually use the agent, and use that to decide what to build next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll Thrive in This Role If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t worry if you don&#39;t tick every box. These are the things that would make you an especially good fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience working as a Software Engineer, with strong TypeScript/Node fundamentals across back end and front end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped agentic or LLM-based software to production, such as an agent, an assistant, or a chat product, and you&#39;ve been the one running it. You&#39;ve debugged failures in real conversations and kept cost and latency in check as usage and models changed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve designed the agent itself: tools and skills, context and prompt engineering, state, streaming, and the agent loop. You know at least one agent framework or runtime well and can say where it works and where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You improve these systems with evidence. Evals, regression sets, tracing, and feedback from real usage tell you whether a change helped, and you use them to decide what to do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep up with what the foundation labs and the wider community are learning about building agents. You try new techniques early and judge which ones make our product better and are worth adopting now, and which should wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take part in deciding what we build. You read the data, talk to customers, and push for what you think matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in a TypeScript monorepo: React and Tailwind on the front end, tRPC, Node.js, MongoDB, and Temporal on the back end. It runs on GCP with Kubernetes, managed through Terraform. The agent is currently built on the Vercel AI SDK, and we run an MCP server alongside it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to know all of it, but hands-on experience building with LLMs is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Your Journey Could Look Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First day:&lt;/strong&gt; Get the app running locally and make your first commit. Your onboarding buddy helps you get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First week:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the engineers, product managers, and designers you&#39;ll work with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the agent end to end: its tools, skills, MCP surface, and how we evaluate it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship a few smaller features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First month:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the wider engineering team and learn how Ledgy works and how customers use it today. This is the background you&#39;ll use for decisions later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make larger contributions and take a bigger part in code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive part of a larger piece of work, such as process, tooling, a new product, or new functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and Design to prove and deepen the value AI adds to the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in architecture and long-term decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;After the first 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a bigger role in shaping where the team is heading. Own key parts of our AI platform and decide where we can add the most value for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and raise the bar. Help teams across Ledgy add AI to what they build, whether that means advising, reviewing, or working alongside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Ledgy&#39;s technical direction, for AI and for everything else we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting to know you (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Meet with someone from our people team to talk about your experience and to ask questions about the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Coding (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; An equity domain problem to solve collaboratively using your preferred language and IDE. We want to see how you think, so this step does not allow AI. But you can freely look up syntax questions if you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Design (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A system design session where you will design an architecture for a problem from the Ledgy domain using a visual tool of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Answer behavioural style questions about your experience, using the STAR method - with a PM and EM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Interview:&lt;/strong&gt; A chance to meet one of our founders and your hiring manager for a 30-minute chat about Ledgy&#39;s mission and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer&lt;/strong&gt; 🎉&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being part of Ledgy means:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge and re-energize with flexible working hours, 25 days of vacation, and up to 40 days of remote work from outside your home country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make space for your own professional development, with a generous yearly learning &amp;amp; development budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will receive a competitive salary + benefits + equity. All salaries are aligned with competitively benchmarked ranges based on work location and levelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For candidates based in London we use a hybrid work model of 2 days in the office per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is Tenable?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenable® is the Exposure Management company. Over 40,000 organizations around the globe rely on Tenable to understand and reduce cyber risk. Our global employees support 65 percent of the Fortune 500, 50 percent of the Global 2000, and large government agencies. Come be part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes Tenable such a great place to work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ask a member of our team and they’ll answer, “Our people!” We work together to build and innovate best-in-class cybersecurity solutions for our customers; all while creating a culture of belonging, respect, and excellence where we can be our best selves. When you’re part of our #OneTenable team, you can expect to partner with some of the most talented and passionate people in the industry, and have the support and resources you need to do work that truly matters. We deliver results that exceed expectations and we win together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your Role:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Regional Sales Director is responsible for leading France &amp;amp; BeneLux sales teams of highly skilled, seasoned sales individuals. The Regional Sales Director will map the course, develop the vision, implement annual plans and is accountable for delivering measurable results that achieves and exceeds revenue and margin targets for 2026 and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your Opportunity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Act as the front-line manager for the French and BeneLux team.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Accurately manage, inspect and report in a predictable manner on all aspects of pipeline development and forecasts for the region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work closely with new as well as established channel partners to generate new business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop go to market plan for your specific region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiations for large complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work closely with leadership for other functions such as Sales Engineering, Channel, finance, legal, R&amp;amp;D and marketing to ensure efficient alignment to regional activities and to enable optimum sales performance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Direct sales responsibility for accounts in the region and attain revenue goal for new product sales.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Initiate, establish and maintain contact with team members, prospects, clients, and partners within assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop recommendations for growth, opportunities for growth, and key target accounts in the assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a complete knowledge of Tenable’s products.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage active field presence by traveling up to 50% of the time across the France and BeneLux regions to meet with clients, partners, and team members.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;​&lt;b&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;10+ years of senior level management experience of direct reports in a fast paced, highly competitive, ever-changing sales environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Min 6 years experience selling Security Products: Vulnerability Management, Continuous Monitoring, IDS/IPS, SIEM, DLP, Compliance, Encryption, access Management, Authentication, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge and understanding on how to sell multi-product software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of MEDDPICC.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Focus on forecast quality and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8+ years in quota carrying sales role with demonstrated success.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience negotiating large complex deals with extremely complex terms, conditions, price pressures and considerations.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Proven track record working with channel and technology partners to build strategic and cooperative sales campaigns together.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong command of English and French.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;History of coordination within an internal set of multi-functional teams such as Sales Engineers, Inside Reps, Field Marketing, Professional Services, and Channel Management to ensure target quotas as achieved and exceeded.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reference-able domain expertise of the French and BeneLux region, accounts, decision makers and channel partner.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Be a coach to your direct team, as well as a keen interest in raising the bar in the entire team covering the region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to accommodate up to 50% travel for regional business needs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;#LI-AV1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the expected salary range for this position in the primary job location, depending on experience and qualifications.&amp;nbsp;Compensation for the role will depend on a number of factors, including the candidate&#39;s qualifications, skills, competencies, location and experience, and may fall outside of the range shown. Employees are also eligible for variable compensation in addition to base pay (commission for sales roles, bonus for non-sales roles), depending on company and individual performance. Tenable also offers a variety of Competitive wellness and financial benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;EU Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€117.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€156.333,33 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We’re committed to promoting Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) at Tenable - through all equal employment opportunity laws and regulations at the international, federal, state and local levels.&amp;nbsp; If you need a reasonable accommodation due to a disability during the application or recruiting process, please contact&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;a ----- ----- for further assistance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tenable Data Consent Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenable is committed to protecting the privacy and security of your personal data. Depending on your location, one or more of the following notices may apply to you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_General_Applicant_Privacy_Notice_FINAL_4-29-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;General Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_CCPA_Notice_Applicants_FINAL_4-29-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_EEA_UK_Applicant_Privacy_Notice_FINAL_6-4-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EU/EEA/UK Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are the platform turning browsing into shopping&lt;/strong&gt;. We connect 200 million shoppers with deals they love while boosting local sales for hundreds of top retailers and brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help consumers save time and money while making smart shopping decisions, and we support retailers and brands in engaging customers from online research to in-store purchases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2024, Shopfully joined forces with the North American company &lt;a href=&quot;https://corp.flipp.com/&quot;&gt;Flipp&lt;/a&gt;, creating a global leader in the sector. Together, we reach 400 million households and serve over 1,000 top retailers and brands across 27 markets, including Europe, Canada, the USA, Latin America, and Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;spark&lt;/strong&gt; your growth with us?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE LOOK FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🦄&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flipp + Shopfully’s Product team focuses on driving adoption and revenue of our products by identifying the biggest market opportunities, building the case for investing in them, and shipping solutions with engineering, all while representing the voice of our merchant customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Product Manager is a senior, commercially minded product leader who already understands digital advertising. This role requires a strong strategic thinker with good business sense and solid hands-on product skills who leads opportunity identification, builds decision-ready business cases, and works with engineering to ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Sales, Engineering, Data, and Marketing teams across markets to align on key business objectives. By combining market insight, customer feedback, and industry trends, you will make sure our products resonate with merchants and drive growth. We’re looking for someone who can ramp up quickly and contribute independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO &lt;/strong&gt;🏄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Understanding and Opportunity Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Marketing, Sales Engineering and customer-facing teams to understand customer needs and prioritize the opportunities that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find the highest-leverage areas to invest in, and weigh customer demand against our resources, capabilities and strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex questions into clear priorities. For example: how do we create more value for retail partners as their strategies move toward e-commerce? How do we find and build opportunities at scale as products launch in new markets?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Cases and Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases that size opportunities, weigh revenue trade-offs, and structure a clear recommendation so leadership can make a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your recommendations, and be ready to explain them and adapt them as you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy for how our products differentiate from competitors in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Finance on pricing and monetization so our offering stays cohesive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Discovery and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with merchants, advertisers, and internal teams to define problems worth solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise ruthlessly, balancing revenue impact, effort, and strategic fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with engineering to define requirements and ship, from alpha and testing through broad launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Marketing on launch timing and readiness, and run retrospectives on past launches to improve future ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignment and Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate cross-functional alignment (Engineering, Data, Sales, Marketing, Content) with a shared focus on goals and timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across markets and levels of seniority, including senior leadership, with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track progress and impact of product initiatives and communicate results clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with industry analysts, partners, and customers, and represent Flipp + Shopfully at conferences and industry events where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL NEED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;🪄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital advertising foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; supply vs. demand, how exchanges, SSPs, and DSPs work, programmatic bidding, pricing models (CPM, CPC, CPV), and fill rate and yield. Ideally gained in ad tech, a retail media network, a publisher, or a marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building business cases: sizing opportunities, weighing revenue trade-offs, and structuring recommendations for decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy: you figure things out, own the outcome and don’t need close management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine excitement about using AI tools and rethinking how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on product skills: discovery, prioritisation, and working with engineering to ship, not only strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management, with the confidence to work across markets and levels of seniority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scrappy, curious and confident approach. You’re hungry to make an impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 At our company, we value diversity and actively encourage it — we believe a variety of perspectives and backgrounds makes us stronger. We focus on potential rather than on having a “perfect” CV. If this role excites you and you believe you could grow into it — even if you don’t tick every single box in the requirements — we’d love to hear from you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎆&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail, CPG, or retail media background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-market experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can speak Italian or German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION 🌐&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have offices in Milan, Berlin, Barcelona, you can benefit from our flexible hybrid model (full remote available), empowering you to work where you&#39;re most effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOURS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;⏰&lt;br&gt;Your manager and several partner teams are in North America, so you’ll need to be flexible about working some later hours, beyond a standard 9-5 CET.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL FIND AT SHOPFULLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🤗&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 An opportunity to thrive in a rapidly scaling multinational company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕶️ A vibrant, informal, and inclusive work environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We champion autonomy, flexibility, and a hybrid work model, empowering you to own your work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 Access to learning opportunities and regular feedback sessions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍓 Enjoy our central, modern offices featuring fresh snacks, coffee (including vegan options!), and ergonomic setups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 Engage in meaningful team events: offsites, happy hours, company parties and celebrations that unite us beyond daily tasks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻We provide all the necessary equipment for you to work effectively and set up your workspace, wherever you are&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧰 Benefit from additional country-specific advantages based on local contracts and practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE &lt;/strong&gt;💜&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of 450 people (and counting!), from 30 different nationalities. We’re on a mission to innovate, and we believe the key to that is seeing the world through a variety of perspectives. That’s why building a more diverse team, as well as bringing in even more talent, is so important for us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TO FEEL AT HOME 🛋️ IN SHOPFULLY YOU NEED 🎯&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
